# rrule, vendored from crates.io and forked for Aperio.
#
# Why a fork: upstream's zones are chrono-tz's, which is unmaintained and
# carries tzdata 2025b; Aperio's zones come from cal-zone (the tzdata bundled
# with jiff-tzdb). Nothing else is meant to change. Fixes from upstream are
# ported by hand; the weekly zone-data watch reports a new upstream release.

upstream = https://github.com/fmeringdal/rust-rrule
commit = 3843456f739d399cfbeff81288c36a66e8e38b83
path-in-vcs = rrule
crates-io = rrule 0.14.0
crate-sha256 = 720acfb4980b9d8a6a430f6d7a11933e701ebbeba5eee39cc9d8c5f932aaff74
license = MIT OR Apache-2.0
licence-files = LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE (the upstream root at that commit; the .crate ships none)

# Left out of the import: src/bin (the cli-tool binary), examples/, the
# features cli-tool and serde's dependencies (serde_with, orig_serde,
# serde_json). The feature `serde` stays declared and empty.
#
# The import commit holds src/ byte-identical to the .crate's src/ without
# src/bin. To check it, unpack rrule-0.14.0.crate (sha256 above) and compare:
#   tar -xzf rrule-0.14.0.crate && diff -r rrule-0.14.0/src <this crate>/src
# at that commit; only src/bin differs.

# Modified files, one line each. Each says so in its first line.
src/lib.rs: drops #![deny(clippy::all)] (the workspace's -D warnings covers
  it, and a crate-level deny overrode the workspace's lint choices) and
  #![warn(missing_docs)] (71 undocumented error variants and fields).
src/core/rrule.rs: clippy useless_borrows_in_formatting (two format! args).
src/iter/counter_date.rs: clippy manual_contains.
src/core/timezone.rs: Tz::Tz holds a cal_zone::Zone instead of a
  chrono_tz::Tz (still Copy); the 594 named constants are gone, Tz::UTC
  (a const) and Tz::named (tzdata's name in exact case) replace them.
src/core/timezone_impl.rs: From<Utc> gives Tz::UTC, From<cal_zone::Zone>
  replaces From<chrono_tz::Tz>, RRuleOffset::Tz holds cal_zone::ZonedOffset.
src/core/datetime.rs: only Zone::UTC writes `Z` (as chrono_tz::UTC did).
src/parser/datetime.rs: parse_timezone through Tz::named; the test zone is
  a function (Tz::named is no const fn).
src/parser/mod.rs, src/tests/rrule.rs, src/iter/utils.rs,
src/validator/validate_rrule.rs: test zones by name instead of constants.
README.md: where the zones come from.
tests/aperio_zones.rs: new, Aperio's own cases for the zones (gap, fold,
  the midnight drop, BYSETPOS, UTC versus Etc/UTC).
